    "content": "All 16 checklist items have been executed and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n**Summary: 13 PASS / 3 FAIL**\n\nThe core knowledge base is solid: module filtering, document detail rendering, reference navigation, section collapse/expand with chevron indicators and the \"expand first\" guard, the 19-node/19-edge knowledge graph with module color coding, zoom controls, and no-results messaging all behaved correctly.\n\nThree defects found:\n\n1. **IX-16 (FAIL)** — Clicking a graph node only highlights it; it never opens the document view. The user must manually click the Documents tab to see the selected document.\n\n2. **FT-10 (FAIL)** — The module filter chosen in Documents silently filters the Favorites view, which has no module filter of its own. With \"UI\" selected, Favorites showed 1 of 3 favorites while the nav badge still read 3. Persistence, live counts, and marker survival across sort/filter all worked correctly.\n\n3. **FT-9 (FAIL)** — Graph panning is non-functional: the transform stays `translate(0, 0)` under both real drags and paced synthetic mouse sequences, despite the SVG advertising `cursor-grab`/`active:cursor-grabbing`. Pan state therefore can never be established or preserved. Document selection, section states, and zoom were all correctly preserved across tab switches.\n\nWorth noting: FT-9 and IX-16 share a root cause with how the graph view integrates with the rest of the app, and FT-10's leak stems from a single filter state being shared across views rather than scoped per view — so these three failures likely reduce to two focused fixes."
  }
}
